   "text": "I read the structure in three parts and wrote the SMILES from them.\n\n**Macrocycle**\n- The left benzene ring carries a nitrile (C\u2261N). Its two ortho substituents are a CF2\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2 arm and a CH2\u2013O\u2013pyridine arm.\n- The CF2\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2 arm ends on a central benzene ring. That ring has the pyridin-2-yl carbon para to the carbon bearing the benzimidazolylmethyl group.\n- The pyridine is 2,6-disubstituted: one position bears the ring oxygen and the other is bonded to the central benzene.\n\n**Benzimidazole**\n- The ring carries a CH2 link to the central benzene at C2 and an oxetan-2-ylmethyl group on N1.\n- It also has a COOH at C6 and an OCH2CH2OCH3 at C4.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- The only drawn stereocentre is the oxetane C2, which has a hashed bond to the CH2N group.\n- The priorities are O > CH2N > ring CH2 > H. With the hashed CH2N pointing back, the H points toward the viewer, so the apparent sense is reversed.\n- O \u2192 CH2N \u2192 ring CH2 appears clockwise, so the true configuration is counterclockwise, which is S.\n- In the SMILES, the neighbour order at the stereocentre is CH2N, H, O, C3. Here `@@` gives S, so I used `[C@@H]`.\n\nSMILES: N#Cc1ccc2c(c1)C(F)(F)COCc1cc(ccc1Cc1nc3c(OCCOC)cc(C(=O)O)cc3n1C[C@@H]1CCO1)-c1cccc(n1)OC2"
